sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Unequal retardation of the growing horn sheath by its adhesion to the bony core can produce the same spiral as unequal growth, and is probably a very important and sometimes the chief factor in horn curvature.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Uneven adhesion of the horn sheath to its bony core can itself produce the spiral";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XIII, “The Shapes of Horns, and of Teeth or Tusks: with a Note on Torsion”; topic “Summary of horn growth”. Scope: horns of hollow-horned ruminants"
}
